  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 145 AM MDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nHigh pressure will remain in control of our weather pattern the rest \nof the weekend and most of next week, meaning a continuation of warm \nand mostly dry conditions. Temperatures will continue to run above \nclimatological norms with peak warmth occurring either today or \nMonday as the ridge amplifies over the region. Daytime temperatures \nduring this timeframe will run around 10 to 15 degrees above normal \nwith valley locations warming into the low to mid-80s. High \nresolution models indicate a shortwave feature working through \nMonday bringing with it isolated convection and very slight chances \nof precipitation. Otherwise, our next chance of precipitation looks \nto be next Saturday when the next trough works through. National \nBlend temperatures return to climatological norms next Saturday and \ndrop more than 10 degrees below normal on Sunday.",
